    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0025" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg13"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845C.00/12–2346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Rangoon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Packer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-12-24">December 24, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>320. Reur 520 Dec 23.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d15-f1"/> In response press request
                    for comment Dept informally and orally released following Dec 21: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“We welcome Mr. Attlee’s invitation Burmese political leaders come London
                            discuss political future Burma. US has many good friends in Burma,
                            including those who gave invaluable assistance our troops North Burma in
                            campaign against Japanese.</p>
                        <p>In Oct 1946 Brit gave to representative Burmese leaders important and
                            responsible posts Burma Govt and it is our confident hope London talks
                            will result in future progress toward agreed goal of full self-govt for
                            that important Asiatic country.”<anchor n="39" xml:id="d15-f2"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d15-f1" n="38" xml:id="d15-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d15-f2" n="39" xml:id="d15-f2-content">
                <p>On January 2, 1947, the Burma Office in London announced acceptance by the
                    Governor of Burma’s Executive Council of the British invitation to send a
                    delegation for discussions in England and stated that the group would be led by
                    the Deputy Chairman of the Council, U Aung San, with talks beginning the week of
                    January 13.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
